{"title":"Triangle Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Triangle Inequality</b> says that in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nondegenerate\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nondegenerate\">nondegenerate</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/4162d82aea6ee3683541a2b46746f9a720469708.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + BC &gt; AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea4c4c07da1bdc02612934456e1527f89a815ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC + AC &gt; AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d283aaa58fcff6d4fa6aa25f00f128696f35c35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC + AB &gt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>That is, the sum of the lengths of any two sides is larger than the length of the third side.\nIn <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Degenerate\" title=\"Degenerate\">degenerate</a> triangles, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Strict_inequality\" title=\"Strict inequality\">strict inequality</a> must be replaced by \"greater than or equal to.\"\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geometric_Form_extended_to_all_polygons\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geometric Form extended to all polygons</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Algebraic_Form\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Algebraic Form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Algebraic_Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Algebraic Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Vector_Form\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Vector Form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Complex_Form\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Complex Form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Introductory_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Intermediate_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Olympiad_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad Problems</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geometric_Form_extended_to_all_polygons\">Geometric Form extended to all polygons</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Geometric Form extended to all polygons\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Triangle Inequality can also be extended to other <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygons</a>.  The lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a25c2f9720d16d7ab307b6766d3539fad0a05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> can only be the sides of a nondegenerate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f9161c78b26608b0c7de2c8a2a4a646ae4b5bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; a_1 + \\ldots + a_{i -1} + a_{i + 1} + \\ldots + a_n = \\left(\\sum_{j=1}^n a_j\\right) - a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"426\" height=\"54\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/6568d2d291215192bc8d87e4baaee03bdbf0b034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1, 2 \\ldots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />.  Expressing the inequality in this form leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7629646829558181aa0af5af76776d975bd45294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_i &lt; P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6a1e93a5823e619bd817c8f3c3a2e648353498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; \\frac{P}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"56\" height=\"37\" />.  Stated in another way, it says that in every polygon, each side must be smaller than the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Semiperimeter\" title=\"Semiperimeter\">semiperimeter</a>. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Algebraic_Form\">Algebraic Form</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Algebraic Form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The algebraic form of the triangle inequality is stated as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f2e83665c30740800a4b9d7ee2e426eb8032a22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left| |a| - |b| \\right| \\le |a \\pm b| \\le |a| + |b|\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Algebraic_Proof\">Algebraic Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Algebraic Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\text{We know that } &amp; x \\le |x|, \\forall x \\in \\mathbb{R}. \\\\\n\\implies &amp; ab \\le |ab| \\\\\n\\implies &amp; 2ab \\le 2|a||b| \\\\\n\\implies &amp; a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\le a^2 + 2|a||b| + b^2 \\\\\n\\implies &amp; (a+b)^2 \\le |a|^2 + 2|a||b| + |b|^2 \\\\\n\\implies &amp; |a+b|^2 \\le (|a| + |b|)^2 \\\\\n\\implies &amp; |a+b| \\le |a| + |b| \\quad \\text{--- (1)}\n\\end{align*}\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Replacing } &amp; b \\text{ by } -b, \\\\\n\\implies &amp; |a-b| \\le |a| + |-b| \\\\\n\\implies &amp; |a-b| \\le |a| + |b| \\\\\n\\therefore &amp; |a \\pm b| \\le |a| + |b| \\quad \\text{--- (2)}\n\\end{align*}\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b597e6fb4c1cb5e6b6bb058e3cec0c96917d278e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a| = |(a-b)+b|\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bdade58e9c35d0c52da00e78b9f50325072f5c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies |a| \\le |a-b| + |b|\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413f702fb93f0d80fbbbade10f149fac134f8f8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies |a| - |b| \\le |a-b| \\quad \\text{--- (3)}\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Similarly,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59fadce6eaaeb56960c2fcfebbe15981dfa99387.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|b| = |(b-a)+a|\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b4b7794b6a8aa3cfe882fedb7e062761e273f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies |b| \\le |b-a| + |a|\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b00ad0505ed72435ed920a998a914b6158749fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies |b| - |a| \\le |a-b|\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/188ccabaa0b6503a5c089adbaf6491bf3b230bd7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies -(|a| - |b|) \\le |a-b| \\quad \\text{--- (4)}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\\text{By (3) and (4), let } &amp; \\alpha = |a| - |b|. \\\\\n-\\alpha \\le |a-b| &amp; \\text{ and } \\alpha \\le |a-b| \\\\\n\\implies -|a-b| \\le &amp; \\alpha \\le |a-b| \\\\\n\\implies |\\alpha| \\le &amp; |a-b| \\\\\n\\implies ||a| - |b|| \\le &amp; |a-b| \\\\\n\\text{Replacing } b \\text{ by } -b, &amp; \\\\\n||a| - |-b|| \\le &amp; |a-(-b)| \\\\\n\\implies ||a| - |b|| \\le &amp; |a+b| \\\\\n\\therefore ||a| - |b|| \\le &amp; |a \\pm b| \\le |a| + |b|\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p><br />\nEquality cases of the above arise under the following conditions\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/0691b9df0dc52053b119964c6ab1a7885575e9f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a + b| = |a| + |b| \\text{ iff } ab \\ge 0, \\text{ i.e., } a \\text{ and } b \\text{ are of the same sign.}\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6cfe4febb66bfb2d86c36a25769c65e7f5fbb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a - b| = |a| + |b| \\text{ iff } ab \\le 0, \\text{ i.e., } a \\text{ and } b \\text{ are of opposite signs.}\\]\" width=\"464\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Vector_Form\">Vector Form</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Vector Form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The triangle inequality can be generalized to vectors in any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-dimensional Euclidean space:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/068018dca2a5973a07fc49464f64d4fb380c231b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\|\\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{v}\\| \\le \\|\\mathbf{u}\\| + \\|\\mathbf{v}\\|\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />\nThis states that the magnitude of the sum of two vectors is at most the sum of their individual magnitudes. Equality holds if and only if one vector is a non-negative scalar multiple of the other (i.e., they point in the same direction).\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80e44547663bc95410b486356480a570f3bbace.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Here, &quot;iff&quot; means &quot;if and only if&quot; as the conditions are of the form &quot;implies and is implied upon&quot;.}\\]\" width=\"710\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Complex_Form\">Complex Form</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Complex Form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The triangle inequality also holds for any two complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f2eefaad556e3b8a7c52cfdb5a292466f451e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1, z_2 \\in \\mathbb{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6abbe6b53dbf0b2bb0ba5986a62013de6fd7651a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|z_1 + z_2| \\le |z_1| + |z_2|\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\nGeometrically, this states that the distance from the origin to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0dbaa906de5df4b2fb8427b154ee14c3ad25d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 + z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> is at most the sum of the distances from the origin to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea31e5c5613f025b5be8aca425d318168491d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea31e5c5613f025b5be8aca425d318168491d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0dbaa906de5df4b2fb8427b154ee14c3ad25d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 + z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> in the complex plane.\n</p><p>Equality holds if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea31e5c5613f025b5be8aca425d318168491d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/29535bc04682b0b477c682ee52dded5983bc41cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> lie on the same ray starting from the origin. Formally, this occurs if:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197d6051c6d4168687ff13ab874eb35da3fe9d3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Arg}(z_1) = \\text{Arg}(z_2)\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />\nor if at least one of the numbers is zero. This can also be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e3278e4e79af78e7ac2a8e1f4c79d04e594dfa87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 \\bar{z_2} \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory_Problems\">Introductory Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\"> 2006 AMC 10B Problem 10</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\"> 2006 AIME II Problem 2</a></li>\n<li>Find the domain of x for which the following equation is satisfied:</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d527ace0c3221a732e8eb3e32d3b2be0470852c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|x| + \\left| \\frac{x}{x-1} \\right| = \\frac{x^2}{|x-1|}\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"44\" />\nSolution- \nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46d577a39078aade5714f0ed761b08f3bb08c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2}{x-1} = x + \\frac{x}{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"150\" height=\"42\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a92bdc95e5f9acff4a09df74d682e226b7beb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8ddc7bb85f11a0c445161260851a0d0820566781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{x}{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"80\" height=\"36\" />. The given equation is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c8ab0b4979adccac75704d94997bf3c4f12809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a| + |b| = |a + b|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>As established in the equality conditions above, this holds if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a6740133910e6e86618ea6fceba885e9556e90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4800767c933da428ec099f6f651e41d6ccd3ef0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\cdot \\left( \\frac{x}{x-1} \\right) \\ge 0 \\implies \\frac{x^2}{x-1} \\ge 0\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"43\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40a92236cec211a3176828810392bfe066b7ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. \nThe solution set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb56ead6c4d5fe7a2af885726142636b128827c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0\\} \\cup (1, \\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate_Problems\">Intermediate Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\"> 2010 AMC 12A Problem 25</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad_Problems\">Olympiad Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Belarus 2002 <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=59933\">Aops Topic</a></li></ul>\n<p>Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0baebc7d737259b31d2b4cc202dfb18d661d53d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />, prove:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2b7ccc620c80325ce20ae5b267d3f8f51a483c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(a+c)^2+(b+d)^2}+\\frac{2|ad-bc|}{\\sqrt{(a+c)^2+(b+d)^2}}\\geq \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}+\\sqrt{c^2+d^2} \\geq \\sqrt{(a+c)^2+(b+d)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"723\" height=\"47\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra\" title=\"Algebra\">Algebra</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality\" title=\"Inequality\">Inequality</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_inequalities\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Geometric inequalities\">Geometric inequalities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">Triangle</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163539\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 281/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9085/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.414      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.414      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2126:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163539 and revision id 284381. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}